WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.152
Full fine-tuning computes gradients and updates the model's trainable weights across the whole network.

00:00:06.152 --> 00:00:13.252
That provides maximum flexibility, but it also requires much more G P U memory, compute, storage,

00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:17.712
and training infrastructure than lightweight adaptation.

00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:23.447
Because so many weights are trainable, the optimizer also needs substantial memory,

00:00:23.447 --> 00:00:26.665
which is one reason full fine-tuning is expensive.
